>
  <p><em>This is a courtesy translation. The <a href="/privacidad/apps/" hreflang="es" lang="es">Spanish version</a> is the original and prevails in case of any discrepancy.</em></p>
  <p>We value the transparency and privacy of our users. This policy describes in general terms how our applications and services handle information. For the <strong>kuxarstudio.com</strong> website, see the <a href="/en/privacy/">site privacy policy</a>.</p>

  <h2>1. Applications and specific policies</h2>
  <p>Each of our applications has different features and its own detailed policy:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Kaku!:</strong> <a href="/en/kaku/privacy-policy/">view privacy policy</a></li>
    <li><strong>BlindNote:</strong> <a href="/en/blindnote/privacy-policy/">view privacy policy</a></li>
  </ul>

  <h2>2. Information collection and third-party services</h2>
  <p>In our applications we use <strong>Google Firebase</strong> services. Depending on the app, these services may collect anonymous technical data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Analytics and performance:</strong> we use Firebase Analytics and Crashlytics to understand errors and improve stability.</li>
    <li><strong>Advertising:</strong> we use Google AdMob to show ads, which may use advertising identifiers from your device.</li>
    <li><strong>Cloud storage:</strong> applications such as Kaku! use Google Firestore to securely sync your progress.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>3. Personal data</h2>
  <p>It depends on each app:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Kaku!</strong> processes your email address (through Google Sign-In) and your progress (completed characters, streaks and statistics), linked to your account, to sync your progress across devices. The data is stored in Google Firestore. You can ask for it to be deleted at any time.</li>
    <li><strong>BlindNote</strong> does not collect or store personally identifiable information (such as emails or names) on our servers. The third-party services it uses (Spotify, AdMob, Firebase Analytics) may process technical identifiers under their own policies.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>In both apps, usage statistics and crash reports are associated with pseudonymised installation identifiers. We do not sell your data to third parties.</p>

  <h2>4. Security</h2>
  <p>We apply industry-standard security measures and Android’s native APIs to ensure that data stored locally or in Firestore remains protected.</p>

  <h2>5. Contact</h2>
  <p>If you have any general question about Kuxar Studio or the handling of your data, write to us at <a href="mailto:admin@kuxarstudio.com">admin@kuxarstudio.com</a>.</p>
</LegalPage>
